// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 12-type-system
// facility: rule.type.typing [T-Call] (an argument where the parameter is a `ref` is a reference); conf.value-for-reference-parameter (D-0232)
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.type-mismatch (static)
//
// `Result::is_ok` takes `ref<Result<T, E>, shared>`. `Ok(1)` is a value,
// whatever `E` turns out to be, so the call is ill-typed: `&r` of a
// binding is what it takes. Before, a constructor whose type parameter
// nothing fixed passed the static pass and faulted when it ran.

import std;

fn main()
{
    bool b = Result::is_ok(Ok(1));
    assert(b);
}
